    {
      "id": "PREP-RATE-2",
      "title": "Prepared replacement is conditional on installed state and configuration",
      "contract": "10021225c can call 1004642e0 before and after other selection steps; later nonnull replacements supersede earlier choices. 1004642e0 rejects a null event, low bit of attribute key 0x63747861, a nonzero phase with zero word from key 0x74616462, failed 100427434, station child count <1, failed configuration predicate 100427220, signed configuration kind >2, missing root/group/prepared object. The station child count is read through 10045ced4 at child+0x28. Fresh child constructor 10045cad0 explicitly initializes this count to zero. Root lookup 1004559b0 compares each group\u2019s 10044fad0 result with the supplied root. Configuration identity comes from 100426e48 (+0x10); kind comes from 100426e08 (+0x68). If (phase & returnedWord)==1, selection calls 1004502c0 and the provider-backed 10043a574 path; otherwise a nonnull event clip/cluster is passed to 10047173c. Calls 10044dc38 and 10045018c precede this branch.",
      "limits": [
        "Numeric attribute keys and configuration fields are identified by bytes/offsets; their user-facing meanings and saved-template eligibility are not established.",
        "This is not a universal ordinary-file path. A freshly unpopulated station fails the count gate.",
        "Signed kind >2 is the inspected rejection; this alone does not reject negative values."
      ],
