      "id": "PREP-RATE-4",
      "title": "A prepared cache miss requests the VstDeck rate product through a provider",
      "contract": "10044fae0 first searches cached collections using the supplied identity. Its fresh construction path calls 10045c73c. That function obtains an interface from the retained provider-container virtual +0x38 and passes it to 10043473c -> 10043394c. The AXtProject constructor stores this interface at +0x1f0 (STP XZR,X24 at 100433a5c). On successful creation, instructions 10044fc74..10044fc80 load VstDeck doubles +0x310/+0x318, FMUL them, and call 10043760c. That helper loads +0x1f0 and, when nonnull, tail-dispatches provider virtual +0xa8 with D0 unchanged.",
      "limits": [
        "This proves a rate-configuration request, not acceptance or a resulting output rate. The concrete provider +0xa8 implementation is unbound.",
        "Cached-hit branches do not repeat this visible request. Later invalidation/host callbacks are not modeled.",
        "Provider-container creation and installed prepared configuration are preconditions; this is not proof that an ordinary one-file event takes this path."
